    schema:datePosted "2026-08-28"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "When it comes to digital communities, The Alliance is leading the way. Product marketing, sales enablement, product-led growth, AI, customer success, CMOs, you name it, we’re home to thriving communities for them all. We connect industry leaders and innovators through unparalleled networking opportunities. We bring together leading minds to share the latest trends, challenges and opportunities facing companies, the tactics and tools needed to drive results, and a forum to make meaningful connections. The Role: Join our dynamic marketing team and step into the world of integrated, multi-channel marketing. Our innovative marketing team supports the company’s growth across diverse product lines, from global events and accredited courses to membership plans and industry-shaping reports. As part of this team, you’ll help drive success across our entire ecosystem, connecting top industry minds, sharing the latest trends, and building meaningful connections. In this role, you will.. Become an Expert in your Audience: learn and develop to manage a specific product portfolio, gaining experience across various product types, including events, education, sponsored products, and community initiatives. Assist in Full-Funnel Campaigns: Help plan and execute marketing campaigns from start to finish, with hands-on involvement in each step—from building data lists to tracking conversions. Multi-Channel Marketing: Assist in developing multi-channel marketing efforts, gaining experience in email, social media, partnerships, and affiliate programs to drive engagement, registrations, and revenue. Create Engaging Content: Write clear, on-brand copy for emails, social posts, and partnerships, helping to manage campaign assets that align with the goals of each product type. Track and Report Performance: Monitor campaign performance metrics, support data collection, and share insights with the team to help inform future strategies and improvements. Collaborate and Learn Across Teams: Work with content, community, product, and sales teams to gain a broad understanding of our marketing efforts and assist in building cohesive campaigns that drive results. Requirements: If the below sounds like you - we’d love to hear from you: You want ownership in your role from the beginning and ready to level up. Confidence to experiment with different tactics, shake up strategy, adapt to new trends, to incorporate business changes, or to bounce back from subpar results You're passionate about using and understanding the data behind WHY things happen and use this to shape your campaigns You take pride in crafting effective and engaging copy whatever the platform You are naturally self-directed, operate at a high cadence, and get stuff done You expertly balance and prioritize your daily to-do's, as well as your short-term and long-term planning You are an extraordinary teammate always willing to jump in and offer support and say \"yes\" to taking on new things Experience with Asana or project management tools a plus (desirable) Experience using ESPs & CRMs, and basic Google Analytics understanding (desirable) Compensation: £26,500 - £30,000 Base salary *depending on previous experience Bonus: Performance Bonus up to 10% yearly _________________________________ Benefits Time off & flexibility 34 days’ paid holiday including UK Bank holidays and a day off on your birthday Flexible working hours: our core hours are 10am–4:30pm, with the flexibility to structure your working day between 8am and 8pm around when you work best Work from where works for you: choose to work remotely within the UK or hybrid from our London office. Our office is always open to the wider team whenever you fancy coming in WFH Kit: a comprehensive tech setup, plus a dedicated WFH equipment budget A well-stocked office: snacks, drinks and fresh fruit available in our London office Health & wellbeing Private Medical and Dental Insurance with Bupa Life Insurance: cover worth 4x your annual salary On-demand therapy & coaching: company sponsored access to therapy and career coaching through Spill Wellness perks: discounts on gym memberships, fitness and wellness classes Cycle to Work & Workplace Nursery schemes Perks at Work: access to a wide range of corporate discounts Monthly flexible benefits allowance through ThanksBen (£50/month in year one, £100/month in year two and £165/month from year three), giving you extra flexibility to spend on the benefits that matter most to you Learning & development A growing personal L&D budget (starting at £500 per year and increasing with tenure to £3,000 per year) Dedicated L&D or volunteering time: one paid day every quarter to invest in your development or support a cause you care about. Unlimited access to our internal Academy: including courses, learning resources and professional certifications Community and Inclusion We are committed to creating a workplace that is free from discrimination and bias, and where everyone has equal opportunities to succeed and contribute. We acknowledge that our work here is never done - and we promise to continue striving for inclusivity every day. If you’re worried you don’t quite hit all the requirements we’ve listed, don’t let that hold you back from submitting your application! Unique backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives are essential for our ability to innovate and grow, so if you think you’d be a great fit then we’d love to hear from you. We are The Alliance - in more ways than one. Compensation: £26.5K – £30K • Offers Bonus • up to 10% Bonus • Base Salary £26.5K – £30K • Offers Bonus • up to 10% Bonus Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
