<https://openknowledgegraphs.com/jobs/live/job/arbeitnow-senior-business-development-manager-dach-berlin-86853> a prov:Entity,
        schema:JobPosting ;
    dcterms:source <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/jobs/source/arbeitnow> ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-08-28T13:20:05+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/jobs/live/occurrence/arbeitnow-senior-business-development-manager-dach-berlin-86853/1>,
        <https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/mute-labs-gmbh/senior-business-development-manager-dach-berlin-86853> ;
    kgjobs:active true ;
    kgjobs:canonicalFingerprint "17330805bc2f164a24ae41e3242b1e3a5c52ca54391a7478bf7fc8578f194b4a" ;
    kgjobs:classification "not_match" ;
    kgjobs:firstSeenAt "2026-08-28T13:20:05+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:lastSeenAt "2026-08-28T13:20:05+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:reconciliationReason "no reviewed first-party candidate" ;
    kgjobs:sourceOccurrence <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/jobs/live/occurrence/arbeitnow-senior-business-development-manager-dach-berlin-86853/1> ;
    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "senior-business-development-manager-dach-berlin-86853" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-28"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "THE JOB The Company: Why mute-labs? At mute-labs, we don’t do \"VC-driven burnout\" or toxic sales floors. We are a self-funded, sustainable team on a mission to bring quiet to the world’s loudest offices. We design and build high-quality acoustic booths that actually make sense for the modern workplace. We don't just sell \"booths\", we sell focus and office sanity. We are looking for a Full-Cycle BDR for the DACH market who wants to own the entire journey, from the first \"hello\" to the final handshake. The Role: Consulting, Not Just Calling You aren't here to read a script. You are here to help companies in Germany, Austria, and Switzerland to design better workspaces. Fresh Inbound Leads: Forget \"smiling and dialing\" into the void. You’ll be the first point of contact for high-quality leads, people who are already curious about what we do. Pipeline Architecture: You’ll identify and reach out to key decision-makers (Facility Managers, HR Leads, Founders), building a pipeline based on quality over quantity. End-to-End Ownership: You’ll identify prospects, lead discovery calls, perform demos, and close the deals. You get the satisfaction of seeing your hard work turn into a physical booth in a client's office. No \"Elbows Out\": We don’t work with commission. Why? Because we want you to do what is best for the client and the team, not your bonus check. We offer a competitive, stable base salary because we trust your intrinsic motivation. A Day in the Life We are an office-first culture. We believe the best sales strategies happen over a shared coffee, not a Slack thread. 09:00 | Morning Vibe: Walk into our high-energy office in Berlin Mitte. Grab a coffee, check the latest leads, and map out your day. 09:30 | The Action Phase: You’re on the phone or video, consulting fresh leads about their office challenges and booking demos. 11:00 | Strategy Huddle: A quick catch-up with Alvaro (Country Manager) or Jarno (Sales Director) to talk about a specific deal or a new market trend you’ve spotted. 12:30 | The Family Table: We eat together. On Fridays, one team cooks for the entire company. Whether it's pasta, tacos, or a local favorite, we bond over food. 14:30 | Market Mastery: You lead discovery demos. You’re listening more than talking, identifying the \"pain points\" of a noisy office. 18:00 | The Close: Wrap up the CRM, update your pipeline, and head out. We respect your \"offline\" time. Pulse & Pints Friday Every Friday, we close the week together. The Pulse: A team huddle to review the numbers, share company updates, and celebrate the people who went the extra mile. The Pints: We transition into the weekend with drinks (alcoholic or 0.0%) and a sense of collective achievement. Our Hiring Process: Fast & Transparent We know you’re talented, so we won’t keep you waiting. The Spark: A quick screening call with Lia to see if our values align. The Market Fit: A deep dive with Alvaro (Country Manager) and Jarno (Sales Director) into your sales DNA. The Commercial View: A conversation with Leah (Head of Commercial) about our growth strategy. The Live Action: A \"Discovery\" role play with the team. No homework - just show us how you handle a real client conversation. The Vision: A final interview with our CEO to discuss the big picture and your future here. Is this you? The Self-Driven Hunter: You don't need a commission check to stay hungry. You take pride in hitting targets and helping the company grow. The Native Communicator: You are fluent in German to effectively navigate the DACH market. The \"Full Cycle\" Mindset: You love the thrill of finding a lead and the pride of closing the deal yourself. The Team Player: You hate working in silos. You want to share your wins and help your teammates with theirs. Are you ready to bring the quiet? If you’re looking for a sales role where you’re treated like a professional, supported by a world-class team, and fueled by a great office culture, we want to meet you. [Apply Now – We’ll get back to you faster than you think!] ABOUT US Here at mute-labs, we aim to enable companies to achieve more by democratizing silence in the workspace. And we’re not like any other Berlin startup you might know: We’re “no tech”: We know how to develop and sell great hardware products with a focus on sound-insulated phone- and meeting booths. We have no investors and we really don’t want any. We've been profitable since day one. We continue to have a steep growth curve – not in employees or coffee cups consumed, but in revenue and profit. We’re not striving for an exit – we’re building a sustainable business for many generations to come. Wondering what it's like to work here? We made a reel about it! Are you as excited about mute-labs as we are? Then we are looking forward to getting to know you! Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Experienced, Full time, Permanent" ;
