    schema:datePosted "2026-08-28"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "Do you want to build frontend software that makes industrial energy systems smarter and more sustainable? At etalytics, we develop AI-powered energy management solutions that help industrial companies reduce energy consumption, CO₂ emissions, and operating costs. Our etaONE® Energy Intelligence Platform combines IoT, data analytics, and artificial intelligence to turn complex energy data into actionable insights. As a Senior Frontend Developer, you will take ownership of complex frontend challenges and help evolve the technical quality of our platform. You will work hands-on with Angular and TypeScript, influence frontend architecture and development standards, and support the team through code reviews, knowledge sharing, and technical guidance. Tasks Develop and enhance scalable, user-friendly frontend features for our etaONE® platform using Angular and TypeScript. Take ownership of complex features from technical concept through implementation, testing, and production. Shape frontend architecture and reusable patterns with a focus on maintainability, performance, and clean system boundaries. Work closely with UX/UI, Product Management, and Backend to turn product requirements into robust and intuitive solutions. Improve code quality through automated testing, thoughtful refactoring, code reviews, and pragmatic technical standards. Identify and resolve complex frontend issues using structured debugging, profiling, and root-cause analysis. Support and mentor other frontend developers through code reviews, knowledge sharing, and technical guidance and contribute to modern development practices, including AI-supported workflows. Requirements You bring a minimum of 4 years of professional frontend development experience and have worked on complex web applications or single-page applications (SPAs). Strong hands-on expertise in Angular and TypeScript enables you to work confidently with modern Angular concepts such as Signals, dependency injection, change detection, and RxJS. You have a solid understanding of frontend architecture, maintainable code, automated testing, performance, and accessibility. You make pragmatic technical decisions and balance software quality, user experience, business needs, and delivery speed. Experience with technologies such as NgRx/SignalStore, NX, Angular Material, Jest, Storybook, Playwright, TanStack Query, or data visualization libraries is an advantage. You communicate confidently in English and collaborate effectively across teams. Benefits: Purpose-driven work: Support industrial companies in becoming more efficient and sustainable Flexibility: Hybrid working with home office options and flexible working hours Team spirit: A supportive, collaborative environment with plenty of room for exchange and cooperation Community: Regular team events and shared activities Work-life balance: 30 days of vacation plus a flexible, agile work culture Well-being: Tax-free benefits card, subsidized local gym membership and the option of a job bike Ready to make an impact? Send us your CV (PDF) together with your earliest possible starting date. We look forward to getting to know you and shaping the future of energy together! Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
