    schema:description "Thiga is a European consulting company whose aim is to make technology a force for differentiation and positive impact. We help businesses drive sustainable growth by embedding a product mindset at the heart of their operations. With a team of 250 specialists, we support top companies and scale-ups in transforming their organizations, upskilling teams, and shaping strategies that turn technology into a true engine for value and innovation. Your Role as a Product Manager Consultant: As a Product Manager Consultant at Thiga, you play a key role in supporting our clients with both strategic and operational Product Management challenges. Your mission goes beyond managing a product: you bring expertise and vision to help our clients evolve in their product maturity. Your Missions: Advise and support companies in structuring and transforming their product organizations (audits, roadmap definition, team coaching). Promote product culture by leading workshops, training teams, and sharing best practices. Define impactful product strategies by helping clients prioritize investments and maximize value creation. Work on diverse missions, from coaching product teams to implementing discovery and delivery frameworks tailored to the client's organization. Contribute to Thiga’s visibility through publications, speaking engagements, and involvement in the product community. Your Impact: You help companies raise their product maturity level with proven, context-adapted methodologies. You’re a transformation accelerator, guiding teams toward greater autonomy and user-centric practices. You encourage innovation and product efficiency by challenging existing practices and offering concrete solutions. Your Profile: You have at least 5-7 years of experience in Product Management, ideally with a varied background (startups, scale-ups, large corporations, consulting). You’re comfortable with both delivery and discovery. You’ve already helped product teams grow in their skills and know how to simplify complex concepts. You love teaching and advising: delivering training, sharing frameworks, and challenging product organizations motivates you. You have an analytical and strategic mindset, enabling you to structure and transform product organizations. You’re curious and keep up with the latest in Product Management and market best practices. Tools like Claude, Replit, Cursor, and Lovable aren’t indie movie titles to you: they’re tabs you've actually opened at least once, probably alongside Figma, Jira, or a Notion doc filled with discovery notes. You are fluent in both English and German, and can work comfortably in multilingual, international environments. Why Join Us? Be at the forefront of transforming companies: You’ll be on the front lines helping businesses improve their product approach. Continuous learning environment: At Thiga, we invest in the development of our consultants through internal training, mentoring, and research projects. Culture of excellence and sharing: We actively contribute to the Product community through events, publications, and regular exchanges. Flexible and stimulating environment: A variety of missions, autonomy, remote work options, and a team of passionate people. Ready to take Product Management to the next level with us? Let’s meet! Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Full-time" ;
